  question="How do you write a good related work section?"
  answer="Organise it by idea, not by paper. Group prior work into three to five themes that matter for your contribution, say what each group established and where it falls short, and end each theme by showing how your work differs. Compare papers with each other rather than summarising them one by one, and cite claims you have checked on the page, not from memory or a summary."
